{"total_count":2,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/4713","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/4713/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/4713/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/4713/events","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/4713","id":1847960026,"node_id":"PR_kwDOELj1_s5XyZNX","number":4713,"title":"feat(`server`): add standalone middleware (experimental)","user":{"login":"jussisaurio","id":22619982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5OTgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22619982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio","html_url":"https://github.com/jussisaurio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":2728304521,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzI4MzA0NTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/labels/@trpc/server","name":"@trpc/server","color":"9BE78E","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":4328853984,"node_id":"LA_kwDOELj1_s8AAAABAgUR4A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/labels/%F0%9F%95%B8%20www","name":"🕸 www","color":"666FF9","default":false,"description":"Stuff to do with the website (`/www` folder)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2023-08-12T11:48:28Z","updated_at":"2023-09-30T18:01:55Z","closed_at":"2023-08-24T10:03:24Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":"resolved","draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/pulls/4713","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/4713","diff_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/4713.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/4713.patch","merged_at":"2023-08-24T10:03:24Z"},"body":"## 🎯 Changes\r\n\r\nProposal/feat: `standaloneMiddleware`\r\n\r\n```\r\n  const projectAccessMiddleware = standaloneMiddleware<{\r\n    ctx: { allowedProjects: string[] }; // defaults to 'object' if not defined\r\n    input: { projectId: string }; // defaults to 'unknown' if not defined\r\n  }>().create((opts) => {\r\n    if (!opts.ctx.allowedProjects.includes(opts.input.projectId)) {\r\n      throw new TRPCError({\r\n        code: 'FORBIDDEN',\r\n        message: 'Not allowed',\r\n      });\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    return opts.next();\r\n  });\r\n```\r\n    \r\nEnables creation of middlewares that are not bound to any particular\r\ntRPC instance; instead they can define a type of `Context`/`Input` that they\r\nexpect, and as long as the preceding middleware chain provides `Context` and `Input`\r\ntypes that are assignable to the middleware's required context type,\r\nthe middleware can be used in the chain. The required context defaults to `object` and the required input defaults to `unknown`.\r\n    \r\nThis commit provides a few tests that demonstrate the usage of\r\nstandalone middlewares in two different tRPC instances.\r\n\r\n## ✅ Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I have followed the steps listed in the [Contributing guide](https://github.com/trpc/trpc/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\r\n- [x] If necessary, I have added documentation related to the changes made.\r\n- [x] I have added or updated the tests related to the changes made.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/4713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/4713/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/3434","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/3434/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/3434/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/3434/events","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/3434","id":1503679210,"node_id":"I_kwDOELj1_s5ZoFLq","number":3434,"title":"feat: extending middlewares","user":{"login":"KATT","id":459267,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTI2Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/459267?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT","html_url":"https://github.com/KATT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":2728304521,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzI4MzA0NTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/labels/@trpc/server","name":"@trpc/server","color":"9BE78E","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2782880104,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzgyODgwMTA0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/labels/%F0%9F%92%A1%20ideas","name":"💡 ideas","color":"bfdadc","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignees":[{"login":"bautistaaa","id":3660667,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjA2Njc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3660667?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bautistaaa","html_url":"https://github.com/bautistaaa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bautistaaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bautistaaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bautistaaa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bautistaaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bautistaaa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bautistaaa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bautistaaa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bautistaaa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bautistaaa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2022-12-19T22:08:39Z","updated_at":"2023-02-15T00:05:32Z","closed_at":"2023-01-31T22:27:17Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":"resolved","sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the feature you'd like to request\r\n\r\nBeing able to create middleware with another middleware as a base middleware\r\n\r\n### Describe the solution you'd like to see\r\n\r\nEither like `.pipe`/`.extend()`/`.use` (or another keyword, idk?)\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nconst fooMiddleware = t.middleware((opts) => {\r\n  return opts.next({\r\n    ctx: {\r\n      foo: 'foo' as const,\r\n    },\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n\r\nconst barMiddleware = fooMiddleware.use((opts) => {\r\n  opts.ctx.foo;\r\n  //        ^? -> 'foo'\r\n  return opts.next({\r\n    ctx: {\r\n      bar: 'bar' as const,\r\n    },\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n\r\nconst proc = t.procedure\r\n  .use(barMiddleware)\r\n  .query(opts => {\r\n     opts.ctx\r\n     //       ^? -> `{ foo: 'foo', 'bar: 'bar', }\r\n  });\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Describe alternate solutions\r\n\r\nNot doing it?\r\n\r\n### Additional information\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### 👨‍👧‍👦 Contributing\r\n\r\n- [X] 🙋‍♂️ Yes, I'd be down to file a PR implementing this feature!","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/3434/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/3434/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}